Damien Neil wrote:

> For example, when you're pushing a boulder down a
> corridor and a monster spawns between it and the
> pits at the end--your only recourse is to destroy
> the boulder, which leaves you stuck without a way
> of creating more.

That's profoundly incorrect.

1) Some wands (except striking, teleport, maybe
polymorph) zap past boulders.

2) Daggers and other weapons and missiles can be
thrown past boulders.

3) Walking away to another part of Sokoban will set
the monster off in a different direction, which may
find it dropping down the open hole "behind" it.

4) Monster movement is somewhat randomized; altering
rest and push repeatedly will allow the PC (slowly)
to push the boulder two spaces from the hole in the
corridor, at some long time after which the monster
may randomly walk into the hole; combine this with 3
to speed the process.

5) The player, at some loss to luck, can squeeze
past the boulder with minimal items in the knapsack,
and melee the monster (risky) or zap it with
teleport.

